s_expandable:!0,note_tweet_results:$R[1563]={__ref:"Tm90ZVR3ZWV0UmVzdWx0czoyMDcxNjI3NTA4NjEzNTcwNTYw"}},Tm90ZVR3ZWV0UmVzdWx0czoyMDcxNjI3NTA4NjEzNTcwNTYw:$R[1564]={__id:"Tm90ZVR3ZWV0UmVzdWx0czoyMDcxNjI3NTA4NjEzNTcwNTYw",__typename:"NoteTweetResults",result:$R[1565]={__ref:"Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwNzE2Mjc1MDg2MTM1NzA1NjA="},id:"Tm90ZVR3ZWV0UmVzdWx0czoyMDcxNjI3NTA4NjEzNTcwNTYw"},"Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwNzE2Mjc1MDg2MTM1NzA1NjA=":$R[1566]={__id:"Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwNzE2Mjc1MDg2MTM1NzA1NjA=",__typename:"NoteTweet",text:"🧵Our unique full-stack approach to AI lets us deliver powerful, cost-efficient products to developers and everyday users. But what exactly does it mean when a technology system is \"full-stack,” and why is it so important to our approach?\n\nWe talked to @rseroter, senior director and chief evangelist at @googlecloud, to break it all down 👇\n\nWhere does the phrase “full-stack” come from, and what does it mean when we’re talking about tech?\n\n@rseroter: The term \"full-stack\" originally came out in software development a decade or so ago — usually in regard to applications. Historically, building an app required multiple specialized teams: a front-end developer to build beautiful user interfaces, a back-end developer to handle server-side logic and a dedicated database team.\n\nThe concept of a \"full-stack engineer\" emerged to describe a developer who could work across all of these functions independently. Instead of constantly handing off components from one person to another, a full-stack engineer could take an idea from a rough concept all the way to a fully running piece of software.",entity_set:$R[1567]={__ref:"client:Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwNzE2Mjc1MDg2MTM1NzA1NjA=:entity_set"},id:"Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwNzE2Mjc1MDg2MTM1NzA1NjA="},"client:Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwNzE2Mjc1MDg2MTM1NzA1NjA=:entity_set":$R[1568]={__id:"client:Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjIwNzE2Mjc1MDg2MTM1NzA1NjA=:entity_set",__typename:"EntitySet",hashtags:$R[1569]={__refs:$R[1570]=[]},symbols:$R[1571]={__refs:$R[1572]=[]},smarttags:$R[157